cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark harness or its reported measurements, please cite the repository."
title: "Benchmarking Efficient Deep Learning Models for Edge AI Deployment"
type: software
authors:
    - name: "Edge AI Deployment Study contributors"
abstract: >-
    A reproducible CPU benchmarking harness that measures accuracy, latency,
    throughput, model footprint and peak memory for efficient convolutional
    architectures under a ladder of deployment optimizations (torch.compile,
    INT8 dynamic and static quantization, quantization-aware training,
    magnitude pruning and ONNX Runtime).
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: MIT
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/raihan-sifat/edge-ai-deployment-study"
keywords:
    - edge ai
    - benchmarking
    - pytorch
    - quantization
    - pruning
    - efficient deep learning
